   186	    - `no_view`: boolean;
   187	    - `reference`: `text` (string), `value` (finite number or null), `items` (list of ids);
   188	    - `implied_outcome`: `text` (string), `low` and `high` (finite numbers or null), `yes_no` (boolean or null), `items` (list);
   189	    - `direction`: above, in_line, below, yes or no;
   190	    - `confidence`: high, medium or low;
   191	    - `decisive_items`: a list;
   192	    - `against`: an object with `text` (string or null) and `items` (list), or null;
   193	    - `reasoning`: a string;
   194	    - `outcome_on_due_day`: present for an event only, absent for a figure; one of that question's rung labels, or null when `no_view`.
   195	  - **When `no_view` is true,** every other field may be null or empty.
   196	  - **Otherwise:**
   197	    - `reference.text`, `implied_outcome.text` and `reasoning` are non-empty;
   198	    - a figure has `low` ≤ `high` (both numbers), `yes_no` null, and `direction` above, in_line or below;
   199	    - an event has `yes_no` a boolean, `low` and `high` null, `direction` yes or no consistent with `yes_no`, and `outcome_on_due_day` consistent
   200	      with `yes_no`;
   201	    - `decisive_items` holds 2 to 6 distinct ids;
   202	    - every id anywhere exists in the packet.
   203	  - **Scale cannot be checked by code** (420 for $420bn passes). A scale slip may show as an A–B disagreement. When both readers make the same
   204	    slip, it passes unnoticed; only the signing page, which prints each range with the question's unit, can show it.
   205	  - **An invalid row** is asked again once by `templates/ask-again.md`, in a new session. That session gets the brief, the packet, that one question
   206	    and the output instruction, and the template lists only the reasons from the closed set `templates/ask-again-reasons.json`. The reader's earlier
   207	    row is not shown, so it judges afresh, as in the established Stage A ask-again. If the row is still invalid, the question is unresolved and goes
   208	    to Alex. A reader unable to cite 2 items is unresolved; it is never pressed to cite more.
   209	
   210	## 5. Reconcile (step 3)
   211	
   212	- **Agreement, by code:**
   213	  - a figure: the two closed ranges [low, high] intersect;
   214	  - an event: `outcome_on_due_day` is equal;
   215	  - both no_view: they agree, and the reference is no_view (not exercised);
   216	  - one side no_view: a disagreement.
   217	- **The proposed reference is reader B's answer** (D262). That the judge (gpt-6-luna, OpenAI) shares reader A's family is a supporting
   218	  observation, not a rule.
   219	- **Every disagreement goes to two third readers,** one of each family, inline and in the closed environments of §4.
   220	  - They see the brief, the packet, the question, the output instruction, and `templates/third-reader.md` with both answers as Answer 1 and Answer
   221	    2, on sides drawn by the manifest's seed. This is the Stage A third readers' practice (`collect_readings.py disputes`).
   222	  - Each rules "1", "2" or **"neither"**, mapped back to A or B by the seed's key. "Neither" carries its own answer in the §4 schema, validated by
   223	    the same code.
   224	  - A missing or invalid ruling is asked again once; if still missing, the question is unresolved.
   225	- **Nothing is replaced automatically.**
   226	
   227	## 6. Alex signs (step 4)
   228	
   229	- **Who signs:** only Alex. Signing cannot be delegated (AGENTS §7.1; D592), because the council has seen the judgements. While he is inactive,
   230	  the line waits.
   231	- **The signing page** `control-reference-v1-for-signing.md` is generated by the fixed generator, in plain English. It shows:
   232	  - D660's three rules and the kept no-reference notes;
   233	  - the 15 questions, with the stripped text recorded;
   234	  - each proposed answer with its items, printed in the question's unit;
   235	  - every disagreement, with both answers and both rulings;
   236	  - every no_view, invalid or unresolved row;
   237	  - every voided output beside its replacement (§0).
   238	
   239	  It shows no judge answer and no chosen rung. The judgement-text check runs on it.
   240	- **The presenting message** is `templates/signing-summary.md`, its English and Chinese lines filled with the counts only. Claude adds no
   241	  recommendation on a disputed question, and any reply to Alex during signing quotes the page only.
   242	- **Agreed questions** (A and B agree under §5) are listed with B's answer as proposed. His one signature over the page confirms them, and he may
   243	  change any of them by the closed set below. **Disputed, invalid or unresolved questions** each need an explicit choice.
   244	- **His choices per question,** a closed set:
   245	  - a **valid** answer of A, of B or of a third reader (an invalid row cannot be picked);
   246	  - his own answer in the §4 schema, which code validates;
   247	  - **leave out**, which makes it no_view;
   248	  - **reject**, which excludes the question; his reason is recorded and its status kept.
   249	- **A disputed, invalid or unresolved question without a choice blocks the freeze.** If Alex declines to sign, nothing is scored, and that is
   250	  recorded.
   251	
   252	## 7. Freeze (step 5)
   253	
   254	- **`control-reference-v1.json`** holds:
   255	  - `reference_version: 1`;
   256	  - both readers' sha256;
   257	  - each question's source (agreed, or Alex's choice in his words);
   258	  - the stripping record;
   259	  - the label model-authored.
   260	- **Its sha** goes to `control-reference-v1.sha256`, the decision record, and a frozen-file test (`tests/test_frozen_control_reference.py`, as
   261	  `test_frozen_rulers.py`). The scorer reads the sha from that file and refuses a mismatch.
   262	- **Never edited.** A later defect becomes a dated correction record, printed with every score.
   263	
   264	## 8. Material shown (step 6, after the freeze)
   265	
   266	- **The brief.** `control-items-brief.md`, written now for review in this folder and fixed in the manifest. It is the items part of
   267	  `control-reader-brief.md` with its rule word for word: "Search the entries for the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a
   268	  related item is". The same-question and same-due parts, and the names "ruler question" and "reader B", are removed.
   269	- **The readers.** Two readers, one of each family, inline and closed as in §4, see each control's reference decisive items and the evidence
   270	  entries from `judge-inputs-v1.json`.
   271	- **The rule is unchanged:** every request on or before 2026-07-14. Its limit is disclosed: an item shown in an earlier request may be absent
   272	  from the last request whose answer is compared (`STAGE_B_READING.md`).
   273	- **Disputes** go to third readers of each family, who rule without the two answers. A split is `unresolved`, reported apart from `not_shown`.
   274	- **A failed or invalid packet** is asked again once; if it still fails, the control is unresolved.
   275	- **Before scoring,** the outputs' shape and the frozen reference's sha are checked. A failure stops the scoring; it does not exclude controls.
   276	
   277	## 9. The count (step 7, `control_reference_count.py`, fixed in the manifest with its tests)
   278	
   279	**Exclusions,** each listed with its reason and never counted:
   280	- not built;
   281	- no judgement on or before 2026-07-14;
   282	- the reference is no_view, left out or rejected;
   283	- fewer than 2 decisive items;
   284	- an item not_shown;
   285	- an item unresolved, reported apart.
   286	
   287	**Agreement:**
   288	- **A figure:** the band of the last judgement's rung, [lo, hi), overlaps the reference's [low, high]. This is the frozen scorer's half-open rule
   289	  (`score_judgement.py`).
   290	- **An event:** the label of the last judgement's rung, resolved from its stored position through the question's rungs, equals the reference's
   291	  `outcome_on_due_day` (D660).
   292	- **"The last judgement"** is the one with the highest `judgement_id` on or before 2026-07-14, as in `control_theses.py` and `score_judgement.py`.
   293	- **The "fewer than 2 decisive items" exclusion** cannot fire under §4's validity rule. It is kept as a guard against a signed own-answer that
   294	  slipped past.
   295	
   296	**The verdict is D428's line:**
   297	- **MET:** at least 8 controls counted, and all but one of them agree.
   298	- **MISSED:** at least 8 counted, and two or more disagree.
   299	- **UNEXERCISED:** fewer than 8 counted. The report names each exclusion's cause.
   300	
   301	**Reported beside the verdict, never changing it (D660):**
   302	- **Null baselines.** Each is paired with the judge on its own available controls. For each, the report prints the controls it covers, the
   303	  judge's agreements there, the baseline's agreements there, and "above", "equal" or "below". A baseline available on no control prints
   304	  "unavailable".
   305	  - **Figures, lookup** (ruler-v1 §1): the rung containing `reference.value`. Unavailable when the value is null or no rung contains it.
   306	  - **Figures, middle** (D660's example): rung 3 of 5. For figures with a stated reference, the ladder puts that value in the middle range (the
   307	    ladder request, line 16). For the others it is the model's own centre, which is disclosed.
   308	  - **Events, always Still open** (D660's example). On a Yes / No event it is always No: the status quo.
   309	- **The line against reader A:** the same counted controls, with A's answer in place of the reference.
   310	  - A's no_view, invalid or unavailable answers are not counted, and the denominator is printed.
   311	  - It is a sensitivity reading: the material shown was checked against the reference's items, not A's.
   312	- **The A–B disagreement rate.**
   313	- **Per matter:** each seed question id (q04, q07, q08, q09, q13, q16, q18) with its counted controls and agreements.
   314	
   315	## 10. Predictions, written before any reader runs
   316	
   317	- **The old reference's 8 of 15 with every item shown is a historical count, not a bound.**
   318	- **An unexercised result** may come from no_view, invalid or unresolved references, missing judgements, unresolved shown checks, or delivery. The
   319	  report names which.
   320	- **A missed result** is specific to this reference, these questions and these stored judgements.
   321	- **Most A–B disagreements will split by family.** On 9 of Stage B's 12 splits, each third reader sided with its own family's first reader. Those
   322	  splits were on judgement verdicts.
   323	
   324	## 11. What it does not measure, and its weak points
   325	
   326	- **Not measured:** whether the right questions were opened (D1); delivery beyond the shown filter (D2); the judge's daily path.
   327	- **Model-authored.** Alex's signature is the human vote, and the noise is printed.
   328	- **One stored run,** on the luna configuration's questions.
   329	  - MET shows the line met on these 15. It does not pass Stage B, which also missed the strictest last-answer reading.
   330	  - MISSED stops the line before further spend (D355).
   331	  - UNEXERCISED names its causes.
   332	- **Tuning exposure.** If a miss leads to a judge change (D263), these 15 become tuning data, and the next application must be on unseen questions.
   333	
   334	## 12. State × event
   335	
   336	| Event | What happens |
   337	|---|---|
   338	| Build refusal | The whole build stops; to the council |
   339	| A judgement-text hit in any participant-facing file | The build stops; to the council |
   340	| A stored input, template, environment or tool version differs from the manifest | The step refuses; to the council |
   341	| The manifest is re-issued after any step | Every dependent artifact (reader outputs, rulings, signature, frozen reference, shown-check outputs) is void; recorded |
   342	| A slot already has a completed or running session | Not launched again |
   343	| A session is void (closed set, §4) | Recorded; one fresh rerun; a second void makes its questions unresolved |
   344	| An interruption mid-step | The step reruns from its last completed predecessor. Outputs are written whole with their sha; a partial output is discarded and recorded |
   345	| An invalid reader row | Asked again once; if still invalid, unresolved |
   346	| A and B disagree | Two third readers |
   347	| A third reader is missing or invalid, or rules "neither" | Missing or invalid: asked again once, else unresolved. "Neither" goes to Alex |
   348	| Alex inactive | The line waits |
   349	| Alex amends | From the closed set, in his words; the page is regenerated and re-signed |
   350	| A disputed, invalid or unresolved question has no choice, or Alex declines | No freeze, nothing scored; recorded |
   351	| The signed reference or the shown-check output fails its sha or shape | Scoring stops; to the council |
   352	| A shown-check session failure, invalid packet or split | Asked again once, else unresolved, reported apart |
   353	| A defect after the freeze | A dated correction record |
   354	| A later run with other questions | A new gold with its own decision (AGENTS §7.1) |
   355	
   356	## 13. Sources of every rule (AGENTS §11)
   357	
   358	| Rule | Source |
   359	|---|---|
   360	| The packet as material | ruler-v1 §1; D658; D659 |
   361	| The brief byte for byte; inline; no file or command | ruler-v1 §2.1; `run_reader_codex.py` |
   362	| 2 to 6 decisive items; fewer than 2 not counted | ruler-v1 §1.5; AGENTS §4 |
   363	| Events on three outcomes; every question counts | D660; ruler-v1 §2 ("一题一个区间，每题都算") |
   364	| Stripping the quoted reference; keeping the unquoted note | D660's words |
   365	| Reader B as the proposed reference | D262 |
   366	| Third readers see both answers on the reference, and neither answer on the shown check | `collect_readings.py disputes`; `control-reader-brief.md` |
   367	| All disputes to Alex; signing his alone | D658; AGENTS §7.1; D592 |
   368	| Figure comparison, threshold, window end | D428; `control_theses.py`; `score_judgement.py` |
   369	| The baselines and their use | D660 (middle, always Still open, reported only); ruler-v1 §1 (lookup) |
   370	| Freeze, correction records, frozen-file test | ruler-v1 §2; D261; `test_frozen_rulers.py` |
   371	| Closed reader environments | D658 ("两组没参与造这个系统的审查者"); ruler-v1 §2.1 |
   372	
   373	## 14. Cost
   374	
   375	The A sessions run on the operator's Codex and the B sessions on the Claude command line. Neither is an API spend. No paid model call of the
   376	pipeline is made.
   377	
   378	## 15. Changes from version 5
   379	
   380	- **Every participant-facing text is written out in `templates/`,** reviewed and fixed in the manifest: the output instruction, the ask-again text
   381	  with its closed reasons, the third-reader text and the signing summary.
   382	- **The population** comes from `mapping-runs.json`'s `questions` map. Each thesis resolves to its view through `clean_ladders` in its Stage B store,
   383	  as `control_theses.py` does; the `views` map is not used. The 15 ids are listed.
   384	- **The leak check:**
   385	  - words are cut on everything that is not a letter or digit;
   386	  - the columns are `reasons`, `reference`, `implied_outcome` and `why_changed`;
   387	  - the permitted source is defined per file and includes checked session outputs and the unstripped rungs;
   388	  - the test covers reader, third-reader, signing and shown-check files with planted leaks.
   389	- **Voided outputs** are printed on the signing page beside their replacements.
   390	- **Attempts:** ask-again and rerun are their own slots.
   391	- **The user-level `CLAUDE.md` content** is checked.
   392	- **The items brief** uses c-ids, one object per control.
   393	- **The files** live under `poc/data/clean-control-reference-2026-11-17/`, and code refuses the frozen ruler's folder. The change of `kind` from
   394	  asset/theme to figure/event is stated.
   395	- **"The last judgement"** is the one with the highest `judgement_id`. The 2-item exclusion is kept as a guard.
   396	
   397	## 15a. Changes from version 4 (kept for the record)
   398	
   399	- **The leak check** is source-aware. It covers the judge's reason, reference, implied outcome and why_changed. It is tested on real inputs and on
   400	  a planted leak, and a hit stops the build.
   401	- **A manifest re-issued after any step** voids every dependent artifact, the signature and the frozen reference included.
   402	- **The reader environments are closed and pinned:**
   403	  - Codex runs with `--skip-git-repo-check`, memories off, and model and effort pinned;
   404	  - Claude runs with no settings, no MCP, no tools and no slash commands, model pinned;
   405	  - both were probed today, and each session's first event is checked against the manifest;
   406	  - the void rule is now a closed set of events;
   407	  - a slot with a completed or running session is not launched again.
   408	- **The stripping rule follows D660's words:** the two quoted forms are removed and the unquoted no-reference note is kept and disclosed. The
   409	  remainder equals `interval_text`. The facts are corrected: 3 stripped, 3 kept.
   410	- **The schema:** `outcome_on_due_day` is absent for figures and null when no_view; the required texts are non-empty; the same scale slip by both
   411	  readers is disclosed.
   412	- **Signing:** agreed questions are confirmed by his one signature; disputed, invalid or unresolved questions need an explicit choice.
   413	- **The items-only brief** is written (`control-items-brief.md`) for review.
   414	- **The "always Yes" baseline is dropped,** for lack of a source. The baselines' sources are listed.
   415	- **The c-ids follow `mapping-runs.json`'s order,** without q23.

