**Version 6 is close, but two contracts still need tightening before the build.** The question lookup now follows the stored Stage B path, and the items brief uses the `c01`–`c15` IDs consistently. [Population](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v6/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v6.md:74), [items brief](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v6/control-items-brief.md:20).

- **The leak check permits the text D660 says to remove.** Version 6 treats the unstripped choices as a permitted source for every participant-facing file. If a generator accidentally puts the removed quotation back into a reader prompt, the eight-word check will allow it because it exists in that source. Check each rendered reader question against the **stripped** question file; allow the removal record only on Alex’s signing page. The same per-stage contract should explicitly cover voided outputs, which the page must show even though the permitted-source list names only outputs that passed checks. [Leak check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v6/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v6.md:119), [voided outputs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v6/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v6.md:32), [D660](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9267).

- **The third reader has no answer for a genuine unresolved choice.** “1,” “2,” and “neither” require the reader to select one answer or assert that neither is supported. If the material supports both different ranges, or the reader cannot distinguish them, the template forces a stronger conclusion than the material warrants. Add an explicit unresolved ruling for Alex, with the source-based reason. This does not exclude a control from the final reference: Alex still chooses at signing. [Third-reader template](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v6/templates/third-reader.md:3).

The event instruction asks for the outcome expected on the due day and applies each choice’s condition; it does not steer toward a particular outcome and follows D660. The ask-again reasons describe shape failures without prescribing an answer, and the retry now has its own slot. [Event instruction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v6/templates/reader-output-instruction.md:3), [retry rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v6/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v6.md:179).

NOT READY: Check rendered reader questions against the stripped inputs and allow third readers to report an unresolved choice.
